## Alternative: Using `argpartition` for Large Collections

For extremely large collections where you only need top N (N << array size), use a selection algorithm:

```rust
use ndarray::Array1;
use std::cmp::Ordering;

fn get_top_n_indices_selection(lst0: &[f64], n: usize) -> Vec<usize> {
    let mut indexed: Vec<(usize, f64)> = lst0
        .iter()
        .enumerate()
        .map(|(idx, &val)| (idx, val))
        .collect();

    let k = n.min(indexed.len());

    // Partial sort: only top N are guaranteed sorted
    indexed.select_nth_unstable_by(k - 1, |a, b| {
        b.1.partial_cmp(&a.1).unwrap_or(Ordering::Equal)
    });

    indexed[..k]
        .iter()
        .map(|(idx, _)| *idx)
        .collect()
}
```

